Source: topology
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Corwin Brust <corwin@bru.st>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), help2man, git <!nocheck>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://gw26.bru.st/
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/inputloop/topology.git -b corwin

Package: topology-www
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: nginx | httpd
Description: draw what you have -- the browser app, as files
 The front door, the drawing app (TopoForge) and its settings pages, under
 /usr/share/topology/www.  Nothing runs: open index.html in a browser, or
 serve the folder.  This is all of topology that a "ceiling = spa"
 machine uses.

Package: topology-perl
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: perl 5.44.0 built for topology, with its CPAN modules
 A perl of its own under /opt/topology/perl, so topology does not depend
 on, or change, the system perl.  Vendored in: Feature::Compat::Class,
 Object::Pad, Future, Future::AsyncAwait, IO::Async and what they need
 (vendor/VENDOR.org in the source says who maintains each, and why it
 was chosen).

Package: topology
Architecture: all
Depends: topology-perl (>= ${source:Version}), adduser, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: git, topology-www
Description: draw what you have, from the git repositories that describe it
 The topology command, the graph API service (topology-api) and the
 settings in /etc/topology.  It fetches the repositories listed in
 /etc/topology/repos.d, reads their TOPOLOGY.md files, and keeps what it
 learns as small files under /var/lib/topology/graph.  Every feature can
 be switched off in /etc/topology/topology.conf.
